IMPORT policy

-- Standing preamble applied to every query below: all conditions unrelated to the
-- stated facts are met, and no exclusion not mentioned is triggered. The agreement
-- is signed and the premium is paid on time (both assumed by the benchmark's own
-- prompt), so every claim below sets `agreement signed` IS TRUE and
-- `premium paid month` IS JUST 0. Every field not discussed in a given question is
-- set to a value that satisfies §1.3 (a compliant, on-time wellness visit and
-- confirmation), raises no §2.1 exclusion, and leaves §3.2's arbitration / waiting
-- period machinery untouched (no dispute has arisen).

-- Q1. will my policy apply if I was hospitalized by burns suffered while doing my
-- duty as a firefighter?
-- Burns are an accidental injury; "doing my duty as a firefighter" is the injury
-- arising out of service as a fire fighter, §2.1(3).
q1 MEANS Claim WITH
    `agreement signed`                           IS TRUE
    `premium paid month`                         IS JUST 0
    `hospitalization month`                      IS 3
    `hospitalization ground`                     IS `Accidental injury`
    `age at hospitalization`                     IS 40
    `causes`                                     IS LIST Firefighting
    `fraud month`                                IS NOTHING
    `misrepresentation month`                    IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit month`                       IS JUST 1
    `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS TRUE
    `written confirmation month`                 IS JUST 2
    `dispute arisen`                             IS FALSE
    `unable to settle month`                     IS NOTHING
    `arbitration commenced month`                IS NOTHING
    `valid arbitration award issued`             IS TRUE
    `written proof of claim month`               IS NOTHING
    `recovery sought month`                      IS NOTHING
    `policy term months`                         IS 12

#EVAL covered q1

