-- Q4. will my policy apply if I was hospitalized due to a fall while traveling
-- abroad and I had given confirmation of my wellness visit 8 months after the
-- policy's effective date?
-- A fall is an accidental injury; being abroad does not exclude coverage (§3.1.1:
-- worldwide, 24 hours a day). The confirmation was supplied at month 8, after the
-- §1.3 7-month deadline, so it was NOT timely. `hospitalization month` is set to 8
-- for narrative consistency with "I had given confirmation ... 8 months after" (the
-- confirmation preceding the hospitalization); its exact value does not change the
-- result, because a confirmation that was actually supplied is checked against the
-- 7-month deadline on its own terms, independent of when the hospitalization fell.
q4 MEANS Claim WITH
    `agreement signed`                           IS TRUE
    `premium paid month`                         IS JUST 0
    `hospitalization month`                      IS 8
    `hospitalization ground`                     IS `Accidental injury`
    `age at hospitalization`                     IS 40
    `causes`                                     IS LIST Other
    `fraud month`                                IS NOTHING
    `misrepresentation month`                    IS NOTHING
    `wellness visit month`                       IS JUST 1
    `wellness visit provider qualified`          IS TRUE
    `written confirmation month`                 IS JUST 8
    `dispute arisen`                             IS FALSE
    `unable to settle month`                     IS NOTHING
    `arbitration commenced month`                IS NOTHING
    `valid arbitration award issued`             IS TRUE
    `written proof of claim month`               IS NOTHING
    `recovery sought month`                      IS NOTHING
    `policy term months`                         IS 12

#EVAL covered q4

-- Q5. will my policy apply if I was hospitalized for punching my own face to show
-- off for my friends and I did not commit fraud or misrepresentation?
-- Judgement call (see NOTES.md): classified as `Accidental injury` rather than
-- `Neither` -- the claimant meant to show off, not to injure himself, so the injury
-- itself was not the intended result of the voluntary act. No cause on the §2.1 list
-- fits "punching my own face", so causes is the catch-all Other.
